+-   **Culled Far Child:** When a node has two intersecting children, but the far child becomes culled during the processing of the near child (due to ray shortening), the algorithm must detect this via `popLevel` to avoid re-entering the near branch [S2, unofficial]. If `level` equals `popLevel` in the single-child branch, it indicates the far child was culled, and `POP()` must be invoked [S2, unofficial].
 -   **Precision:** Care must be taken to ensure that equal $t$ values after a restart do not cause re-entering already processed branches, leading to infinite loops [S2, unofficial].
 
